 "title": "LM2665 switched-capacitor voltage doubler and divider, 40 mA, SOT-23-6",
 "source": {
  "document": "SNVS009H",
  "revision": "SNVS009H, revised March 2016",
  "pages": 22
 },
 "summary": "A CMOS charge pump with no inductor: two capacitors and a start-up Schottky diode turn a 2.5 V to 5.5 V supply into roughly twice that voltage at up to 40 mA. Connected the other way round it halves an input of 1.8 V to 11 V. The oscillator runs at 160 kHz (the switches at 80 kHz), the output looks like 2 × V+ behind about 12 Ω, it draws 650 µA running and 1 µA in shutdown, and it comes in a six-pin SOT-23.",
 "key_figures": [
